        "email": "30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-10T06:52:29Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(app,ui): a refused generation marks the spot it names\n\n#261 part 2, by the triage's middle ground: a refusal does not draw a\npartial path, it draws the place it is about. A generator refusal can\ncarry one spot (GenError::At, built with GenError::invalid_at); run_job\ncarries it to world through the op's frame, the generate command keeps\nit (CommandError::MachiningAt), and the UI marks it in the viewport with\na gouge-coloured cross while the refusal stands. The op page's refusal\nline becomes a link that frames it. Nothing is generated or cached, so\nnothing refused can post. The located errors read exactly like the\nplain ones, so no message changes.\n\nFirst adopters are the refusals that already quoted a point: Face's\nnarrow strip between two holes, the drill cycle's R-plane, counterbore,\nbore-fit and centre-cutting doors, Bore's and Thread's counterbore and\nfit doors, and the plunge law. The cross-hole spindle frame moves the\nspot by the same shift it applies to the sentence.\n\nGenError moves to machining2d/gen_error.rs (face.rs re-exports it).\n\nRefs #261\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
