      "message": "feat(app,motion): drilling refusals mark the hole they are about\n\n#677, the #261 part 2 follow-up: the drilling refusals that quote a\nhole now name it with GenError::invalid_at, so the viewport marks it\nand the op page's refusal line frames it.\n\n- Axial drill: flute reach, holder, shank fit and the R plane mark the\n  hole at the material top the law measured.\n- Cross drill: flute reach and finished-part mark the modelled mouth;\n  the kernel's plunge-axis and bottom-above-entry doors and the raw\n  stock's plunge-direction door mark the local mouth, which in_world\n  carries to world (to_raw_mouths now passes through in_world too).\n- Lathe axial drill: off-axis and wider-than-bore mark the mouth; past\n  the bar's end marks the floor.\n\nThe listed sites that name no spot say why in a one-line comment\n(collect-time stitch fork, turning meridian stations, size/angle\nrefusals). No sentence changes for an on-origin cross drill.\n\nFixes #677\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
